          "text": "Hebrew “sons of Israel,” a collective designation for Israel’s people. The Masoretic Text has “all that his sons were doing to all Israel,” followed by “and that they were lying with the women who served at the entrance to the tent of meeting” (“served” may also mean “assembled”). The shorter ending is reconstructed in 4QSamᵃ from its surviving text and space and is reflected in the B-based Greek text; other Greek witnesses have longer forms. The earliest wording remains uncertain.",
          "reason": "textual_variant"
        }
      ]
